From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 10:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] RFC (DO NOT SUBMIT): mm: add lightweight reclaim policy hook in MGLRU path

/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

Introduce a policy check in the MGLRU (Multi-Gen LRU) scan path to
prioritize or deprioritize pages based on the VMA semantic class.

- VM_SEMANTIC_STREAMING: Treat as "old" generation to accelerate reclaim.
- VM_SEMANTIC_REUSE: Treat as "young" generation to protect from reclaim.
- VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL: Prioritize for eviction even without pressure.

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index [hash]..[hash] 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -200,6 +200,18 @@ static bool lru_gen_scan_folios(struct lruvec *lruvec, struct scan_control *sc,
 	/* ... existing MGLRU logic ... */
 }
 
+/*
+ * RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION
+ * Hook for semantic-aware reclaim decision.
+ * This would be called during page walking or folio isolation.
+ */
+static int get_semantic_priority(struct vm_area_struct *vma)
+{
+	if (vma->vm_flags & VM_SEMANTIC_REUSE)
+		return RECLAIM_PROTECT;
+	if (vma->vm_flags & (VM_SEMANTIC_STREAMING | VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL))
+		return RECLAIM_ACCELERATE;
+	return RECLAIM_NORMAL;
+}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_MEMCG
 /* ... */
 #endif
